  <data name="MacroHelp" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Macros
- Edit: right-click a macro in the tray menu.
- Send via menu: left-click inserts the text and sends it (text + Enter).
- Send without Enter: left-click + Shift (or Alt) sends the text WITHOUT a trailing Enter.
- Hotkeys: Ctrl+F1, Ctrl+F2, Ctrl+F3 each open a picker popup listing the ten macro titles of that
  profile (fixed, independent of which profile is shown in the tray menu). Press a digit (1-9, 0
  for the tenth) to send that macro, or Escape / click elsewhere to cancel. Enter follows the send
  by default; hold Shift or Alt while pressing the digit to suppress it.

Macro profiles
- Three named sets of ten macros each, for different characters or scenarios.
- The first entry of the macro menu names the active profile and expands to the others. This
  "active" profile only affects what the tray menu displays/edits - not which profile Ctrl+F1..F3
  address (those are always fixed to profile 1/2/3).
- Switch (tray view): Macros -&gt; [active profile] -&gt; left-click another profile.
- Rename: Macros -&gt; [active profile] -&gt; "Rename active profile".
- Reset: "Reset active profile" clears the name and all ten macros of the active profile.
  Profiles cannot be removed - there are always exactly three.
- Import and export refer to the active profile unless "Export all profiles" is chosen.

Macro variables
- Macro text may contain {date}, {time}, {day}, {username}, {clipboard} and {input}.
- {day} is the full weekday name in German (e.g. "Montag"), regardless of UI language.
- {input} or {input:Your question} asks for a value right before sending.
- The input dialog is multi-line: Enter inserts a line break, Ctrl+Enter sends, Esc aborts.
- Cancelling discards the whole send.

Media viewer
- Clicking an image or video in Grok opens it in its own window, placed on the left at full
  screen height while Wrok fills the rest. Videos play muted in an endless loop.
- Alternatively: right-click the media -&gt; "Copy image address", then press Ctrl+Ö.
- Ctrl+Ö without a usable clipboard reopens the last media item. Images are cached
  locally for this and need neither network nor an active session.
- Inside the window: Esc closes, + / - and the mouse wheel zoom, Ctrl+F fits,
  Ctrl+S saves, Ctrl+P pins. Drag with the left button to pan.

Boss key
- Ctrl+Space minimizes the window instantly; press again to restore it.
- An open media window is hidden along with it, even when pinned, and returns pinned as before.
- The inactivity timer and closing via the window's X behave the same way.
- Logging off, shutting down or an update, however, really close Wrok instead of parking it.

Tray menu
- Settings -&gt; App: inactivity, macro import/export, start with Windows,
  password saving, proxy, check for updates.
- Settings -&gt; Grok: opens Grok's own settings page.
- Tools: rate limits, open image, delete data.

Delete data
- Tools -&gt; "Delete data" offers two options:
  "Clear cache only" removes images and scripts; you stay signed in.
  "Delete all" additionally removes cookies and login data - you will be signed out - as well
  as the last opened image together with its stored address.
- An extra checkbox clears all macro profiles. Unchecked by default.
- Not affected: window size, inactivity timeout and the remaining program settings.
- Useful for display errors, login problems, or when a clean session is needed.

Updates
- At startup (at most once a day) Wrok checks whether a newer version exists and then shows a
  tray notice plus a menu entry linking to the release page. Nothing is downloaded; the update
  itself goes through WinGet or the installer.
- Check manually: in the info dialog (About Wrok), click "Check for updates". Turn it off under
  Settings -&gt; App -&gt; Check for updates. The check contacts GitHub.

Troubleshooting / Tips
- If text is not sent: make sure the page is fully loaded and the input field is visible.
- F12 opens the WebView2 developer tools (DOM and console).
- Zoom the page: Ctrl + Plus/Minus/0 or Ctrl + mouse wheel. The zoom level is remembered.
- Messages and errors are written to %LOCALAPPDATA%\Wrok\logs\app.log

Brief overview of operation
- Click and hotkey behave the same: insert the text, then send by clicking the send button or
  by a real Enter. Some web editors ignore synthetic keyboard events, so Wrok falls back to a
  genuine keystroke from the operating system when needed.</value>
